The MICOPAM 2025 conference, dedicated to Professor Manuel López-Pellicer, will be held from 8 to 12 September 2025 in Osijek, Croatia. It is organized by the School of Applied Mathematics and Informatics, J. J. Strossmayer University of Osijek, Croatia, the Faculty of Civil Engineering, University of Zagreb, Croatia, and Akdeniz University, Turkey.

The conference aims to bring together leading researchers in pure and applied mathematics and related fields to present their latest findings, exchange innovative ideas, address current challenges, foster future collaborations, and strengthen professional interactions.

Invited speakers:

Manuel López-Pellicer, Universitat Politècnica de València, Spain;

‪Abdelmejid Bayad, Université Paris-Saclay, France;

Gradimir V. Milovanović , Serbian Academy of Sciences and Arts, Serbia;

Julije Jakšetić, University of Zagreb, Croatia;

Santiago Emmanuel Moll-López, Universitat Politècnica de València, Spain;

Yilmaz Simsek, Akdeniz University, Turkey.

Further information can be found on the conference website: 
https://micopam.com/
.

4th Workshop on Optimal Control of Dynamical Systems and Applications will be held 26 – 28 Feb 2025 in Villany, Hungary. Workshop is organized by Osijek Mathematical Society and School of Applied Mathematics and Informatics, J. J. Strossmayer University of Osijek.

This workshop aims to provide a coherent set of lectures that will adequately clarify the mathematical aspects of the (optimal) control of dynamical systems and applications. The intent is to generate fruitful scientific exchanges related to the following topics: model order reduction methods, optimization and applications that arise in the study of dynamical systems.

Plenary speakers:

Tobias Breiten, Technische Universität Berlin, Germany; 

Zlatko Drmač, Department of Mathematics, University of Zagreb, Croatia; 

Cecilia Pagliantini, Universita di Pisa, Italy.

The workshop has more than 20 invited lectures.

The organizing committee members are 

Ion Victor Gosea, Max Planck Institute for Dynamics of Complex Technical System, Magdeburg, Germany; 

Serkan Gugercin,  College of Science at Virginia Tech, USA;

Zoran Tomljanović, School of Applied Mathematics and Informatics, University of Osijek, Croatia;  

Matea Ugrica Vukojević, School of Applied Mathematics and Informatics, University of Osijek, Croatia.

More information can be found on the 
workshop website
.

First Transnational Project Meeting within project GAMMA was held on the 19th and 20th of November 2020. The organizer of this virtually held meeting was J. J. Strossmayer University of Osijek – Department of Mathematics, which is also the coordinator of this project.The meeting was attended by members of the team of the Department of Mathematics and team members responsible for coordination and organization of project activities from other partner organizations.

First Transnational Project Meeting within project GAMMA was held on the 19th and 20th of November 2020. The organizer of this virtually held meeting was J. J. Strossmayer University of Osijek – Department of Mathematics, which is also the coordinator of this project. The meeting was attended by members of the team of the Department of Mathematics and team members responsible for coordination and organization of project activities from other partner organizations. At the beginning of the first day, all partner organizations briefly introduced themselves, after which the presentation of contractual obligations under the project was given. On the second day of the meeting, topics related to Project management and implementation were discussed. 

